I wrote the hidden suite in `packages/core/test/hidden-categories-check/`, in three files: `facts.test.ts`, `rules.test.ts` and `categories.test.ts`. `npx tsc -p tsconfig.test.json` reports no errors. Against the current stubs all 102 tests fail with `not implemented`. While checking that, one test (`PRIORITY_RANKS` has the six keys) passed against the stub, so I changed it to also go through `factsFor`.

**Checked against a correct implementation:** to make sure the tests aren't wrong, I wrote a throwaway JavaScript implementation of the spec in the scratchpad, outside the repo. The public and hidden suites together pass in full against it. That run caught one arithmetic mistake in my own test (a date that was 999 days from now, not 1000), which I fixed.

**Checked against shortcuts:** I then made small broken versions of that implementation, each a shortcut that passes the public suite. The hidden suite fails every one that actually changes behaviour:
- looking up priority names without guarding against built-in object names, so `"constructor"` doesn't rank `"high"`;
- `votes || 0`, which turns `NaN` into 0;
- comparisons where a `NaN` threshold passes;
- treating a missing comment count as 0;
- accepting `true` or arrays as thresholds;
- treating `enabled: 0` as disabled;
- falling back to the label when the only clause is `""`;
- taking a sprint's earliest date from its start and end together, instead of start first;
- not merging thresholds for a disabled category;
- lower-casing the rest of the reason;
- listing Quietly wanted's demand signals in the order of its defaults rather than its rule;
- caching classifier results per facts object;
- adding the year only before a hard-coded 2026;
- sorting the issue's releases in place;
- measuring against a hard-coded `now`.

Things I deliberately left untested because the spec doesn't decide them:
- what `factsFor` returns for dates when `now` is invalid;
- whether `describe` is called on a signal that didn't match;
- the first-letter rule when a reason starts with a space or a non-ASCII letter;
- what a current sprint whose state is `"closed"` adds to `closedSprintCount`.

102 tests, in 3 files.

Open in the spec: none
